                  <bindingDesc resp="#BCBB">
                     <binding notAfter="1500" notBefore="1400">
                        <p>A composite binding, of early boards with later covering:</p>
                        <p>15th century? (contemporary with manuscript?): wood boards, narrow inside bevel, rounded corners, with grooves for two broad straps at fore-edge of 
                           upper board and possible traces of bosses at lower board</p>
                     </binding>
                     <binding notAfter="1700" notBefore="1500">
                        <p>16th century or 17th century?, <placeName key="place_1000080">Italian</placeName>?: later covering of thin red silk, undecorated, 
                           not allowing for the boards’ clasps or bosses; spine lost; edges gilt, gauffered; paper flyleaves with anchor watermark</p>
                     </binding>
                     <binding when="1952">
                        <p>20th century, 1952, Bodleian: rebacked in red leather
                        </p>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
